    "field": "Decadal climate prediction",
    "problem": "Traditional climate model ensemble averages fail to simulate the early-2000s global warming hiatus because they cannot correctly phase the naturally-occurring internal climate variability, specifically the Interdecadal Pacific Oscillation (IPO), which was a primary contributor to the observed slowdown.",
    "method": "The paper shows that applying initialized decadal climate prediction, with models started from observed mid-1990s climate states, could have successfully simulated the early-2000s global warming hiatus by correctly capturing the transition to a negative phase of the Interdecadal Pacific Oscillation.",
    "task": "The task is to assess whether initialized decadal climate prediction models, if applied retrospectively in the 1990s, could have successfully simulated the early-2000s global warming hiatus by capturing the negative phase of the Interdecadal Pacific Oscillation that contributed to the slowdown.",
